# EXPECT_ERROR_CODES_EXACT: CE1001
# EXPECT_DUMP_SHIR: test_err_shir_name_unresolved.shir
#
# the SHIR dump of a name with no declaration. The scope pass reports CE1001 and records
# the name as unresolved. SHIR has no node for such a name, so lowering gives an error
# hole with the name of the AST class and the codes that it stands for, and the compile
# goes on to the typecheck pass. Strict mode never stops on this hole: a program with a
# name that has no declaration always has an error, so the diagnostic of the program is
# CE1001, one of the codes of the hole.

fn main() i32:
    let i32 total = 40 + 2
    return totl - total
